<hr>
<p>The next number is 3. Notice that with the introduction of 3, number 2 s=
hould no longer be considered a candidate. This is because it=E2=80=99s now=
 impossible for 2 to be the next largest number of any value to its left. S=
ince 3 is both larger and further to the left, it will always be prioritize=
d over 2 as the next largest number. So, let=E2=80=99s remove 2 from the ca=
ndidates list, as well as any other candidate that=E2=80=99s less than or e=
